VIE\n\n\nBASE_URL = 'https://m.itv.com/playlist'\n\ndef make_webpage(video_attrs, json_ld=None, title='Test Episode Title', synopsis='A test synopsis'):\n    ...\n\ndef make_playlist(...):\n    ...\n```\n\nHmm, maybe simpler to define module-level constants and a runner helper.\n\nLet me write a helper that sets up an ITVIE with monkeypatched methods and records calls:\n\n```python\nclass _FakeCalls(object):\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.webpage_url = None\n        self.playlist_url = None\n        self.playlist_data = None\n        self.playlist_headers = None\n        self.m3u8_calls = []\n        self.json_ld_calls = []\n\n\ndef _install_fakes(monkeypatch, ie, webpage, playlist, search_json_ld_result=None, json_ld_result=None, m3u8_formats=None):\n    calls = _FakeCalls()\n\n    def fake_download_webpage(url, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        calls.webpage_url = url\n        return webpage\n\n    def fake_download_json(url, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        calls.playlist_url = url\n        calls.playlist_data = kwargs.get('data')\n        calls.playlist_headers = kwargs.get('headers')\n        return playlist\n\n    def fake_extract_m3u8(url, video_id, ext=None, *args, **kwargs):\n        calls.m3u8_calls.append({'url': url, 'video_id': video_id, 'ext': ext, 'kwargs': kwargs})\n        return list(m3u8_formats or [{'url': url, 'ext': ext or 'mp4', 'format_id': kwargs.get('m3u8_id')}])\n\n    def fake_search_json_ld(webpage_, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        return search_json_ld_result if search_json_ld_result is not None else {}\n\n    def fake_json_ld(json_ld, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        calls.json_ld_calls.append(json_ld)\n        return json_ld_result\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_download_webpage', fake_download_webpage)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_download_json', fake_download_json)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_extract_m3u8_formats', fake_extract_m3u8)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_search_json_ld', fake_search_json_ld)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_json_ld', fake_json_ld)\n    return calls\n```\n\nWait \u2014 `monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_download_webpage', ...)` sets an instance attribute; monkeypatch will remove it on teardown. Good \u2014 no state pollution.\n\nHmm, one concern: `monkeypatch.setattr` on an instance attribute that doesn't exist \u2014 monkeypatch requires the attribute to exist by default (`raising=True`). Since these are class methods, `hasattr(ie, '_download_webpage')` is True (found on class), so setattr on the instance works and teardown deletes the instance attribute. Good.\n\nNow the main test:\n\n```python\ndef test_real_extract_full(monkeypatch):\n    webpage = u'''...'''\n    playlist = {...}\n    ie = ITVIE()\n    calls = _install_fakes(monkeypatch, ie, webpage, playlist, json_ld_result={'title': 'Episode Name'})\n    result = ie._real_extract('https://www.itv.com/hub/a-test-show/2a1234a')\n\n    assert result['id'] == '2a1234a'\n    assert result['title'] == 'Test Episode Title'  # depends on merge_dicts precedence!\n    ...\n```\n\nHmm, the title: base dict has title from og:title; info (from _json_ld mock) has title 'Episode Name'. merge_dicts precedence determines the result. Let me wait for get_info on merge_dicts.\n\nFrom youtube-dl utils.py (I'm fairly confident now):\n\n```python\ndef merge_dicts(*dicts):\n    def merge_dict(dst, src):\n        for key, value in src.items():\n            if value is not None:\n                if key in dst and isinstance(dst[key], dict) and isinstance(value, dict):\n                    merge_dict(dst[key], value)\n                else:\n                    dst[key] = value\n\n    res = {}\n    for d in dicts:\n        merge_dict(res, d)\n    return res\n```\n\nHmm wait, that means later dicts override. But I recall the docstring: \"Merge the values of all dicts into a single dict. The values of the dicts take precedence in the order they are passed\" \u2014 hmm, ambiguous. Let me actually recall the real code:\n\