ript[^>]+type=([\"\\']?)application/ld\\+json\\1[^>]*>(?P<json_ld>.+?)</script'\n```\n\nMy script: `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{...}</script>` \u2014 matches, group json_ld = the JSON text. `_parse_json` parses it. Good.\n\nBut wait \u2014 in test 1's webpage, there's also the `<div id=\"video\" ...>` before the script. JSON_LD_RE only matches script tags with ld+json type. Good.\n\nAlso note: `_search_regex` with `(?is)` flags embedded. Fine.\n\nNow \u2014 `_parse_json(json_ld_str, video_id, fatal=False)` \u2014 the parsed object is a dict. `json_ld.get('@type') == 'BreadcrumbList'` \u2014 yes.\n\nOne subtlety: `_parse_json` might apply `transform_source`? No, default None. It might strip... fine.\n\nAnother subtlety: in test 1, the JSON-LD string contains `\"itemListElement:\"` \u2014 valid JSON. Good.\n\nNow, about `_search_json_ld` being mocked \u2014 its real signature: `_search_json_ld(self, html, video_id, expected_type=None, **kwargs)`. My fake: `fake_search_json_ld(html, video_id, *args, **kwargs)`. The call: `self._search_json_ld(webpage, video_id, default={})` \u2192 html=webpage, video_id=video_id, kwargs={'default': {}}. Fine.\n\n`_json_ld` real signature: `_json_ld(self, json_ld, video_id, fatal=True, base=base_url)` \u2014 hmm, `base=base_url`? There's a module-level `base_url`? Actually in youtube-dl, `_json_ld(self, json_ld, video_id, fatal=True, base=base_url)` where `base_url` is a global in InfoExtractor module? I recall `base_url = 'http://schema.org'` defined at module level in extractor/common.py. Yes! In common.py: `base_url = 'http://schema.org'`. So `_json_ld(item, video_id, fatal=False)` \u2192 json_ld=item, video_id, fatal=False, base default. My fake: `fake_json_ld(json_ld, video_id, *args, **kwargs)` \u2014 fine.\n\nNow, ITVIE instantiation: `ITVIE()` \u2014 `InfoExtractor.__init__(self, downloader=None)`. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: `InfoExtractor` might have `__init__` requiring downloader with params for `_sort_formats`... mocked. `_download_webpage` mocked. OK.\n\nWhat about `self._match_id` \u2014 uses `self._VALID_URL` \u2014 ITVIE has it. But wait, in newer youtube-dl, `_match_id` calls `self._match_valid_url(url)` which uses `self._VALID_URL`. ITVIE defines `_VALID_URL`. Fine.\n\nHmm, also `_match_id` might call `self._match_valid_url(url).group('id')` \u2014 needs 'id' group in _VALID_URL. ITVIE's has `(?P<id>...)`. Verify via get_info.\n\nNow \u2014 the `geo_verification_headers` \u2014 let me think about whether it could hit `self._downloader.params`. In youtube-dl common.py:\n\n```python\n    def geo_verification_headers(self):\n        headers = {}\n        geo_proxy = self._get_geo_proxy()\n        if geo_proxy:\n            headers['X-Forwarded-For'] = geo_proxy\n        return headers\n```\n\nand\n\n```python\n    def _get_geo_proxy(self):\n        \"\"\"Return the location of a random proxy used by _download_webpage etc.\n        Returns None if there is no proxy.\"\"\"\n        if self._downloader:\n            return self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass_proxy')\n```\n\nHmm, no... Actually I recall `_get_geo_proxy` is in InfoExtractor:\n\n```python\n    def _get_geo_proxy(self):\n        \"\"\"Return the location of a random proxy used by _download_webpage etc.\n        Returns None if there is no proxy.\"\"\"\n        if self._downloader:\n            return self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass_proxy')\n```\n\nHmm, I genuinely don't remember. get_info will tell. If it needs `self._downloader`, I'll set `ie._downloader` to a simple object with `params = {}`. Or monkeypatch `geo_verification_headers`... but that skips real line 62 execution? No \u2014 line 62 `headers = self.geo_verification_headers()` still executes (calling the mock). But better to let real code run if safe. I'll adapt based on get_info.\n\nAlright \u2014 also `InfoExtractor.__init__` \u2014 does it require downloader? `def __init__(self, downloader=None)`. Fine.\n\nLet me also double check `extrac