as 'description': None \u2192 filtered out of info dict (real _json_ld filters None values!) \u2192 info has no 'description' \u2192 merged description = 'A test synopsis'. \u2713.\n\nWait \u2014 in test 1, the TVEpisode item has no 'description' key \u2192 `unescapeHTML(None)` \u2192 None \u2192 info['description'] = None \u2192 filtered \u2192 info = {'episode': 'Episode Name', 'title': 'Episode Name'}. \u2713.\n\n39. Hmm, one more: `get_element_by_class('episode-info__synopsis', webpage)` \u2014 let me make sure the div content extraction works. youtube-dl's `get_element_by_class` \u2192 `get_element_by_attribute('class', 'episode-info__synopsis', html)`. The implementation:\n\n```python\ndef get_element_by_attribute(attribute, value, html, escape_value=True):\n    \"\"\"Return the content of the first tag with the specified attribute and value.\"\"\"\n    value = re.escape(value) if escape_value else value\n    m = re.search(r'''(?xs)\n        <([a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+)\n         \\s+(?:[a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+\\s*=\\s*\"[^\"]*\"\\s*)*?  # optional attributes\n         %s\\s*=\\s*(?P<_q>[\"'])(?P<value>%s)(?P=_q)\n    ''' % (re.escape(attribute), value), html)\n    if not m:\n        return None\n    ...\n    content = html[m.end():]\n    m = re.search(r'</\\s*%s' % m.group(1), content, re.M)  # hmm\n```\n\nSomething like that \u2014 it finds the tag then content until closing tag. For `<div class=\"episode-info__synopsis\">A test synopsis</div>` \u2192 returns 'A test synopsis'. Then clean_html \u2192 'A test synopsis'. \u2713.\n\nHmm, actually the newer youtube-dl get_element_by_class:\n\n```python\ndef get_element_by_class(class_name, html):\n    \"\"\"Return the content of the first tag with class attribute containing `class_name`\"\"\"\n    return get_element_by_attribute('class', class_name, html)\n```\n\nHmm \u2014 \"containing\"? There was a version using `class=\"[^\"]*\\bclass_name\\b[^\"]*\"`. Either way, exact single class matches. \u2713.\n\n40. Now, let me also double check `_html_search_meta(['og:title', 'twitter:title'], webpage)`: `_meta_regex('og:title')`:\n\n```python\ndef _meta_regex(self, prop):\n    '''Return meta tag regex for given property name'''\n    return r'(?is)<meta[^>]+(?=(?:itemprop|property|name)=[\"\\']%s[\"\\'])[^>]+content=[\"\\']([^\"\\']+)[\"\\']' % re.escape(prop)\n```\n\nRoughly. My meta: `<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Test Episode Title\">` \u2014 matches: `<meta[^>]+(?=(?:itemprop|property|name)=[\"\\']og:title[\"\\'])[^>]+content=[\"\\']([^\"\\']+)[\"\\']`. Hmm \u2014 `<meta[^>]+` then lookahead `(?=property=\"og:title\")` then `[^>]+content=\"Test Episode Title\"`. Let me trace: `<meta` then `[^>]+` greedy... the lookahead must match at some position. `[^>]+` backtracks so that lookahead position is at ' property=\"og:title\"...' \u2014 wait the lookahead is `(?=(?:itemprop|property|name)=[\"\\']og:title[\"\\'])` \u2014 at position after `<meta` + some chars. `[^>]+` = ' ' then lookahead at 'property=\"og:title\"' \u2713 then `[^>]+content=` \u2014 after the lookahead position (which doesn't consume), `[^>]+` matches 'property=\"og:title\" ' then `content=\"Test Episode Title\"` \u2713. Group 'content' = 'Test Episode Title'. \u2713.\n\nThen `_html_search_regex` returns res.strip() \u2192 'Test Episode Title'. \u2713.\n\n41. Now let me also handle: in test 2, webpage has og:title 'Second Title'. \u2713.\n\n42. What about `compat_str` in merge_dicts \u2014 fine.\n\n43. Let me write the final code now.\n\n```python\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"Coverage tests for ITVIE._real_extract (youtube_dl/extractor/itv.py, lines 55-150).\n\nAll network access and the non-deterministic format sorting are stubbed out\nwith monkeypatch, so the tests exercise the extractor's own logic only and\nleave no global state behind.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\n\nfrom youtube_dl.extractor.itv import ITVIE\n\n\ndef _webpage(video_attrs, json_ld_scripts=(), title='Test Episode Title',\n             synopsis='A test synopsis'):\n    \"\"\"Build a fake ITV hub page.\"\"\"\n    attrs = ' '.join('%s=\"%s\"' % (k, v) for k, v in video_attrs.items())\n    parts = [\n        '<!DOCTYPE html><html><head>',\n        '<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"%s\">' % title,\n        '</head><body>',\n        '<div id=\"video\" %s></div>' % attrs,\n    ]\n    if synopsis is not None:\n        parts.append('<div class=\"episode-info__synopsis\">%s</div>' % synopsis)\n    for script in json_ld_scripts:\n        parts.append('<script type=\"application/ld+json\">%s</script>' % script)\n    parts.append('</body></html>')\n    return '\\n'.join(parts)\n\n\nclass _FakeDownloader(object):\n    \"\"\"Minimal stand-in for the YoutubeDL downloader (params only).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.params = {}\n\n    def report_warning(self, msg, *args, **kwargs):\n        pass\n\n\nclass _Recorder(object):\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.webpage_urls = []\n        self.playlist_requests = []\n        self.m3u8_calls = []\n        self.sort_calls = []\n\n\ndef _make_ie(monkeypatch, webpage, playlist):\n    \"\"\"Create an ITVIE with network access and format sorting stubbed out.\"\"\"\n    rec = _Recorder()\n\n    def fake_download_webpage(url, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        rec.webpage_urls.append(url)\n        return webpage\n\n    def fake_download_json(url, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        rec.playlist_requests.append({\n            'url': url,\n            'video_id': video_id,\n            'data': kwargs.get('data'),\n            'headers': kwargs.get('headers'),\n        })\n        return playlist\n\n    def fake_extract_m3u8(m3u8_url, video_id, ext=None, **kwargs):\n        rec.m3u8_calls.append({\n            'url': m3u8_url,\n            'video_id': video_id,\n            'ext': ext,\n            'kwargs': kwargs,\n        })\n        return [{\n            'url': m3u8_url,\n            'ext': 'mp4',\n            'format_id': kwargs.get('m3u8_id'),\n            'protocol': 'm3u8_native',\n        }]\n\n    def fake_sort_formats(formats, *args, **kwargs):\n        rec.sort_calls.append(list(formats))\n\n    ie = ITVIE()\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_downloader', _FakeDownloader())\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_download_webpage', fake_download_webpage)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_download_json', fake_download_json)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_extract_m3u8_formats', fake_extract_m3u8)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_sort_formats', fake_sort_formats)\n    return ie, rec\n```\n\nWait \u2014 `monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_downloader', _FakeDownloader())` \u2014 `_downloader` exists (None) \u2192 OK.\n\nHmm \u2014 one issue: `_search_json_ld` and `_json_ld` are REAL. In test 1, `_search_json_ld` \u2192 `_json_ld([breadcrumb], ...)` \u2014 real. Fine.\n\nBut wait \u2014 there's a potential problem with real `_search_json_ld` in tests where the webpage has NO ld+json script (test 2): `json_ld_list = []` \u2192 `if json_ld:` (empty list) \u2192 False \u2192 `if default is not NO_DEFAULT: return default` \u2192 {}. \u2713 No downloader interaction. Good.\n\nAnd in `_json_ld` real \u2014 does it touch `self._downloader`? Looking at the source: no. \u2713.\n\n`_parse_json` on failure \u2192 `self.report_warning(...)` \u2014 InfoExtractor.report_warning \u2014 let me think whether it needs downloader... \n\n```python\ndef report_warning(self, msg, video_id=None):\n    idstr = '' if video_id is None else format_field(video_id, template=' %s')\n    if self._downloader:\n        self._downloader.report_warning(...)\n    else:\n        self.to_stderr(...)\n```\n\nHmm, actually I recall:\n\n```python\n    def report_warning(self, msg, video_id=None, only_once=False):\n        ...\n        msg = ('WARNING:' ...)\n        if self._downloader:\n            self._downloader.report_warning(msg)\n        else:\n            self.to_stderr(msg)\n```\n\nWhatever \u2014 my JSON is valid, so _parse_json never fails. And I have a fake downloader with report_warning anyway. \u2713.\n\nNow the tests:\n\n```python\ndef test_real_extract_full_pipeline(monkeypatch):\n    url = 'https://www.itv.com/hub/liar/2a4547a0012'\n    video_id = '2a4547a0012'\n    webpage = _webpage(\n        {\n            'data-video-playlist': 'https://m.itv.com/playlist/2a4547a0012',\n            'data-video-hmac': 'aabbccdd',\n        },\n        json_ld_scripts=(\n            '{\"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement:\": ['\n            '{\"item:\": {\"@type\": \"TVEpisode\", \"name\": \"Episode Name\"}}]}',\n        ),\n    )\n    playlist = {\n        'Playlist': {\n            'Video': {\n                'Base': 'https://base.example.com/',\n                'Duration': 'PT00H02M33S',\n                'MediaFiles': [\n                    {'Href': 'video.m3u8'},\n                    {'Href': 'video.mp4'},\n                    {},\n                ],\n                'Subtitles': [\n                    {'Href': 'https://subs.example.com/en.vtt'},\n                    'not-a-dict',\n                    {'Href': None},\n                ],\n            },\n        },\n    }\n    ie, rec = _make_ie(monkeypatch, webpage, playlist)\n\n    result = ie._real_extract(url)\n\n    # Lines 55-56: video id matched from the URL, page downloaded from it.\n    assert result['id'] == video_id\n    assert rec.webpage_urls == [url]\n\n    # Lines 60-67: playlist URL taken from data-video-playlist; request\n    # headers carry the upper-cased hmac and the ITV vod playlist content type.\n    assert len(rec.playlist_requests) == 1\n    request = rec.playlist_requests[0]\n    assert request['url'] == 'https://m.itv.com/playlist/2a4547a0012'\n    assert request['video_id'] == video_id\n    assert request['headers'] == {\n        'Accept': 'application/vnd.itv.vod.playlist.v2+json',\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n        'hmac': 'AABBCCDD',\n    }\n    payload = json.loads(request['data'].decode('utf-8'))\n    assert payload['user'] == {\n        'itvUserId': '', 'entitlements': [], 'token': ''}\n    assert payload['device'] == {\n        'manufacturer': 'Safari',\n        'model': '5',\n        'os': {'name': 'Windows NT', 'version': '6.1', 'type': 'desktop'},\n    }\n    assert payload['client'] == {'version': '4.1', 'id': 'browser'}\n    assert payload['variantAvailability'] == {\n        'featureset': {\n            'min': ['hls', 'aes', 'outband-webvtt'],\n            'max': ['hls', 'aes', 'outband-webvtt'],\n        },\n        'platformTag': 'dotcom',\n    }\n\n    # Lines 100-115: Href-less media file skipped, Base prefixes the Href,\n    # m3u8 handled by _extract_m3u8_formats, others appended verbatim.\n    assert rec.m3u8_calls == [{\n        'url': 'https://base.example.com/video.m3u8',\n        'video_id': video_id,\n        'ext': 'mp4',\n        'kwargs': {\n            'entry_protocol': 'm3u8_native',\n            'm3u8_id': 'hls',\n            'fatal': False,\n        },\n    }]\n    assert result['formats'] == [\n        {\n            'url': 'https://base.example.com/video.m3u8',\n            'ext': 'mp4',\n            'format_id': 'hls',\n            'protocol': 'm3u8_native',\n        },\n        {'url': 'https://base.example.com/video.mp4'},\n    ]\n    assert len(rec.sort_calls) == 1\n    assert rec.sort_calls[0] == result['formats']\n\n    # Lines 117-127: valid subtitle kept; non-dict and Href-less entries skipped.\n    assert result['subtitles'] == {\n        'en': [{'url': 'https://subs.example.com/en.vtt', 'ext': 'vtt'}]}\n\n    # Lines 130-141: _search_json_ld yields nothing for the BreadcrumbList,\n    # so the fallback parses it, finds the TVEpisode item, injects @context\n    # (line 139) and extracts info through _json_ld (line 140).\n    assert result['episode'] == 'Episode Name'\n\n    # Lines 143-150: base metadata merged with the JSON-LD info.\n    assert result['title'] == 'Test Episode Title'\n    assert result['description'] == 'A test synopsis'\n    assert result['duration'] == 153\n```\n\nWait \u2014 `result['duration'] == 153` \u2014 parse_duration('PT00H02M33S') \u2192 0*3600 + 2*60 + 33 = 153.0. `153.0 == 153` \u2713.\n\nHmm \u2014 one thing to double check in test 1: `_search_json_ld` real \u2192 `_json_ld([breadcrumb], video_id, fatal=False, expected_type=None)`. breadcrumb = {'@type': 'BreadcrumbList', 'itemListElement:': [...]}. `'@context' in e` \u2192 False \u2192 loop continues \u2192 return {}. \u2713 \u2192 default {} returned.\n\nFallback: `_search_regex(JSON_LD_RE, webpage, 'JSON-LD', '{}', group='json_ld')` \u2192 matches the script \u2192 group json_ld = the JSON text. `_parse_json(text, video_id, fatal=False)` \u2192 dict. `json_ld.get('@type') == 'BreadcrumbList'` \u2713. `json_ld.get('itemListElement:')` \u2192 the list. ile = {'item:': {...}} \u2192 `ile.get('item:')` \u2192 item dict \u2192 '@type' == 'TVEpisode' \u2713 \u2192 item['@context'] = 'http://schema.org' \u2192 `info = self._json_ld(item, video_id, fatal=False) or {}` \u2192 real _json_ld \u2192 {'episode': 'Episode Name', 'title': 'Episode Name'} \u2192 truthy \u2192 info = that. break.\n\nmerge_dicts(base, info): base has title 'Test Episode Title' \u2192 wins. info adds 'episode'. \u2713.\n\nresult['episode'] == 'Episode Name' \u2713 \u2014 and this proves line 139 executed (without @context, _json_ld would skip the item and return {}).\n\nHmm wait, actually \u2014 let me double-check `_json_ld`'s guard once more from the source I got:\n\n```python\nfor e in json_ld:\n    if '@context' in e:\n        item_type = e.get('@type')\n        if expected_type is not None and expected_type != item_type:\n            continue\n        if item_type in ('TVEpisode', 'Episode'):\n            episode_name = unescapeHTML(e.get('name'))\n            info.update({'episode': episode_name, 'episode_number': int_or_none(e.get('episodeNumber')), 'description': unescapeHTML(e.get('description'))})\n            if not info.get('title') and episode_name:\n                info['title'] = episode_name\n            ...\n```\n\n\u2713. And the final `return dict(((k, v) for k, v in info.items() if v is not None))` \u2192 {'episode': 'Episode Name', 'title': 'Episode Name'}. \u2713.\n\nTest 2:\n\n```python\ndef test_real_extract_data_video_id_without_base_or_subtitles(monkeypatch):\n    url = 'https://www.itv.com/hub/show/2b5678b'\n    video_id = '2b5678b'\n    webpage = _webpage(\n        {'data-video-id': video_id, 'data-video-hmac': 'ddeeff00'},\n        title='Second Title', synopsis=None)\n    playlist = {\n        'Playlist': {\n            'Video': {\n                'Duration': '153',\n                'MediaFiles': [{'Href': 'https://cdn.example.com/video.mp4'}],\n            },\n        },\n    }\n    ie, rec = _make_ie(monkeypatch, webpage, playlist)\n\n    result = ie._real_extract(url)\n\n    assert result['id'] == video_id\n    # Line 60: no data-video-playlist -> data-video-id used as playlist URL.\n    assert rec.playlist_requests[0]['url'] == video_id\n    # Line 104: no Base -> Href used verbatim; line 107: not m3u8 -> plain format.\n    assert rec.m3u8_calls == []\n    assert result['formats'] == [{'url': 'https://cdn.example.com/video.mp4'}]\n    # Line 118: no Subtitles key -> empty subtitle dict.\n    assert result['subtitles'] == {}\n    # Lines 130-135: no JSON-LD at all -> default '{}' parses to a falsy value.\n    assert 'episode' not in result\n    assert result['title'] == 'Second Title'\n    assert result['description'] is None\n    assert result['duration'] == 153\n```\n\nTest 3:\n\n```python\ndef test_real_extract_non_breadcrumb_json_ld_and_empty_media_files(monkeypatch):\n    url = 'https://www.itv.com/hub/show/2c1111c'\n    webpage = _webpage(\n        {'data-video-playlist': 'https://m.itv.com/playlist/2c1111c',\n         'data-video-hmac': 'aa'},\n        json_ld_scripts=('{\"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Just a page\"}',))\n    playlist = {'Playlist': {'Video': {}}}\n    ie, rec = _make_ie(monkeypatch, webpage, playlist)\n\n    result = ie._real_extract(url)\n\n    # Line 100: missing MediaFiles -> empty formats list.\n    assert result['formats'] == []\n    assert rec.m3u8_calls == []\n    # Line 118: missing Subtitles -> empty subtitle dict.\n    assert result['subtitles'] == {}\n    # Line 135: JSON-LD present but not a BreadcrumbList -> item loop skipped.\n    assert 'episode' not in result\n    assert result['title'] == 'Test Episode Title'\n    assert result['description'] == 'A test synopsis'\n    # Line 148: missing Duration -> parse_duration(None) is None.\n    assert result['duration'] is None\n```\n\nTest 4:\n\n```python\ndef test_real_extract_search_json_ld_result_skips_fallback(monkeypatch):\n    url = 'https://www.itv.com/hub/show/2d2222d'\n    webpage = _webpage(\n        {'data-video-playlist': 'https://m.itv.com/playlist/2d2222d',\n         'data-video-hmac': 'bb'},\n        json_ld_scripts=(\n            # First script: a BreadcrumbList that the (skipped) fallback would\n            # otherwise mine for a TVEpisode named 'Fallback Episode'.\n            '{\"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement:\": ['\n            '{\"item:\": {\"@type\": \"TVEpisode\", \"name\": \"Fallback Episode\"}}]}',\n            # Second script: _search_json_ld extracts info from this one.\n            '{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"TVEpisode\", '\n            '\"name\": \"Search Episode\"}',\n        ))\n    playlist = {'Playlist': {'Video': {'MediaFiles': [{'Href': 'y.mp4'}]}}}\n    ie, rec = _make_ie(monkeypatch, webpage, playlist)\n\n    result = ie._real_extract(url)\n\n    # Line 131: non-empty JSON-LD info -> BreadcrumbList fallback skipped,\n    # so the fallback's 'Fallback Episode' never surfaces.\n    assert result['episode'] == 'Search Episode'\n    assert result['title'] == 'Test Episode Title'\n    assert result['formats'] == [{'url': 'y.mp4'}]\n```\n\nWait \u2014 hmm, in test 4, `_search_json_ld` real: json_ld_list = [breadcrumb, tvep] (both scripts). `_json_ld([breadcrumb, tvep], ...)`: breadcrumb no @context \u2192 skip; tvep has @context \u2192 TVEpisode \u2192 info = {'episode': 'Search Episode', 'episode_number': None, 'description': None} + title 'Search Episode' \u2192 filtered \u2192 {'episode': 'Search Episode', 'title': 'Search Episode'}. Non-empty \u2192 returned. Line 131: `if not info:` \u2192 False \u2192 fallback skipped. \u2713.\n\nmerge: base title wins \u2192 'Test Episode Title'; episode 'Search Episode' added. \u2713.\n\nHmm \u2014 but wait, would the fallback (if it ran) really produce 'Fallback Episode'? `_search_regex(JSON_LD_RE, ...)` returns the FIRST match = breadcrumb script \u2192 BreadcrumbList \u2713 \u2192 itemListElement: \u2192 TVEpisode 'Fallback Episode' \u2192 info = {'episode': 'Fallback Episode', 'title': 'Fallback Episode'} \u2192 merged episode = 'Fallback Episode'. So yes, the assertion distinguishes. \u2713.\n\nTest 5:\n\n```python\ndef test_real_extract_breadcrumb_items_without_tvepisode_info(monkeypatch):\n    url = 'https://www.itv.com/hub/show/2e3333e'\n    webpage = _webpage(\n        {'data-video-playlist': 'https://m.itv.com/playlist/2e3333e',\n         'data-video-hmac': 'cc'},\n        json_ld_scripts=(\n            '{\"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement:\": ['\n            '{},'\n            '{\"item:\": {\"@type\": \"WebPage\"}},'\n            '{\"item:\": {\"@type\": \"TVEpisode\"}}]}',\n        ))\n    playlist = {'Playlist': {'Video': {'MediaFiles': [{'Href': 'z.mp4'}]}}}\n    ie, rec = _make_ie(monkeypatch, webpage, playlist)\n\n    result = ie._real_extract(url)\n\n    # Lines 136-138: entries without 'item:' or without a TVEpisode item are\n    # skipped; line 140: the nameless TVEpisode yields no info ('or {}').\n    assert 'episode' not in result\n    assert result['title'] == 'Test Episode Title'\n    assert result['formats'] == [{'url': 'z.mp4'}]\n```\n\nWait \u2014 in test 5, the TVEpisode item has NO name \u2192 real `_json_ld(item)`: episode_name = unescapeHTML(None) = None \u2192 info.update({'episode': None, 'episode_number': None, 'description': None}) \u2192 title not set \u2192 return filtered {} \u2192 falsy \u2192 `or {}` \u2192 info = {}. \u2713 covers line 140's right side.\n\nHmm \u2014 but wait: does `_json_ld` return {} or... `if not json_ld: return {}` \u2014 json_ld is the item dict (truthy) \u2192 continue. `info = {}` ... loop: e = item, '@context' in e \u2713 (line 139 added it) \u2192 item_type 'TVEpisode' \u2192 expected_type None \u2192 processes \u2192 all None \u2192 `video = e.get('video')` \u2192 None \u2192 `if expected_type is None: continue` \u2192 loop ends \u2192 `return dict(... if v is not None)` \u2192 {}. \u2713.\n\nAnd the first ile `{}` \u2192 `ile.get('item:')` \u2192 None \u2192 `or {}` \u2192 item = {} \u2192 `item.get('@type')` \u2192 None \u2260 'TVEpisode' \u2192 skip. Second ile: item = {'@type': 'WebPage'} \u2192 not TVEpisode \u2192 skip. Third: TVEpisode \u2192 line 139-140. \u2713 covers 137 both branches, 138 both branches, 140 or-right.\n\nBut \u2014 hmm, wait: `_search_json_ld` runs FIRST on this webpage: breadcrumb script without @context \u2192 `_json_ld([breadcrumb])` \u2192 {} \u2192 default {} \u2192 fallback runs. \u2713.\n\nTest 6:\n\n```python\ndef test_real_extract_breadcrumb_without_item_list(monkeypatch):\n    url = 'https://www.itv.com/hub/show/2f4444f'\n    webpage = _webpage(\n        {'data-video-playlist': 'https://m.itv.com/playlist/2f4444f',\n         'data-video-hmac': 'dd'},\n        json_ld_scripts=('{\"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\"}',))\n    playlist = {'Playlist': {'Video': {'MediaFiles': [{'Href': 'w.mp4'}]}}}\n    ie, rec = _make_ie(monkeypatch, webpage, playlist)\n\n    result = ie._real_extract(url)\n\n    # Line 136: BreadcrumbList without 'itemListElement:' -> 'or []' -> no loop.\n    assert 'episode' not in result\n    assert result['title'] == 'Test Episode Title'\n    assert result['formats'] == [{'url': 'w.mp4'}]\n```\n\nHmm \u2014 wait, in test 6, `_search_json_ld` real: json_ld_list = [breadcrumb] \u2192 `_json_ld([breadcrumb])` \u2192 no @context \u2192 {} \u2192 default {} \u2192 fallback \u2192 line 135: BreadcrumbList \u2713 \u2192 line 136: `json_ld.get('itemListElement:')` \u2192 None \u2192 `or []` \u2192 empty loop \u2192 info stays {} \u2192 merge \u2192 no episode. \u2713.\n\nNow \u2014 hold on, I should double-check `_search_json_ld`'s behavior when `_json_ld` returns {} \u2014 `if json_ld: json_ld = self._json_ld(...)` \u2014 json_ld here is the LIST [breadcrumb] (truthy) \u2192 calls _json_ld \u2192 {} \u2192 `if json_ld:` \u2192 {} falsy \u2192 `if default is not NO_DEFAULT: return default` \u2192 {}. \u2713.\n\nNow \u2014 one more consideration: in tests 3-6, the playlist Video has no 'Duration' \u2192 `parse_duration(None)` \u2192 None (isinstance check fails) \u2192 result['duration'] is None. \u2713 (test 3 asserts this).\n\nAlso \u2014 `result['description']` in tests 4-6: synopsis div present \u2192 'A test synopsis'. I assert in some.\n\nNow \u2014 is there any issue with `_real_extract` being called directly vs `extract`? `_real_extract` doesn't call `self.report_extraction` etc. Fine.\n\nOne more potential gotcha: `ITVIE()` \u2014 `InfoExtractor.__init__(self, downloader=None)`:\n\n```python\ndef __init__(self, downloader=None):\n    self._downloader = downloader\n```\n\nThat's it in old versions. \u2713.\n\nAnd `_match_id` is a classmethod \u2014 `self._match_id(url)` works.\n\n`_VALID_URL_RE` caching: `if '_VALID_URL_RE' not in cls.__dict__: cls._VALID_URL_RE = re.compile(cls._VALID_URL)` \u2014 sets class attribute. Idempotent across tests. Not pollution (it's a cache that would exist anyway). OK.\n\nNow \u2014 about `monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_download_webpage', fake)`: `_download_webpage` is a method on InfoExtractor; hasattr(ie, '_download_webpage') \u2192 True \u2192 setattr on instance OK; teardown deletes instance attr. \u2713.\n\nWait \u2014 one thing: `_download_webpage` in InfoExtractor might be defined... yes it is (calls _download_webpage_handle). \u2713 exists.\n\n`_extract_m3u8_formats` exists \u2713. `_sort_formats` exists \u2713. `_download_json` exists \u2713. `_downloader` \u2014 instance attr from __init__ \u2713.\n\nNow \u2014 the fake `_download_json` signature: the real call passes `data=` and `headers=` as kwargs. My fake: `def fake_download_json(url, video_id, *args, **kwargs)` \u2192 kwargs has data, headers. \u2713.\n\nThe fake `_extract_m3u8_formats`: real call `self._extract_m3u8_formats(href, video_id, 'mp4', entry_protocol='m3u8_native', m3u8_id='hls', fatal=False)` \u2192 my fake `def fake_extract_m3u8(m3u8_url, video_id, ext=None, **kwargs)` \u2192 m3u8_url=href, video_id, ext='mp4', kwargs={'entry_protocol', 'm3u8_id', 'fatal'}. \u2713.\n\nHmm \u2014 wait, is `ext` passed positionally 'mp4'? Yes: `self._extract_m3u8_formats(href, video_id, 'mp4', ...)`. \u2713.\n\nNow \u2014 assertion `rec.m3u8_calls == [{... 'kwargs': {'entry_protocol': 'm3u8_native', 'm3u8_id': 'hls', 'fatal': False}}]` \u2014 dict equality \u2713.\n\nNow \u2014 one more thought about test 1's `result['formats']` exact equality: the m3u8 format dict is exactly what my fake returned (sort mocked, no mutation). The mp4 format: `{'url': 'https://base.example.com/video.mp4'}` \u2014 sort mocked \u2192 no 'ext' mutation. \u2713.\n\nAnd `rec.sort_calls[0] == result['formats']` \u2014 list of same dicts \u2192 \u2713.\n\nNow \u2014 potential issue: `merge_dicts` \u2014 base dict includes 'formats': formats (the list). info has no 'formats'. merged['formats'] = the list. \u2713.\n\nLet me also double check the base dict keys: id, title, formats, subtitles, duration, description. Plus info: episode, title. Merged: id, title (base), formats, subtitles, duration, description, episode. \u2713.\n\nNow \u2014 one more check on `_webpage` helper: attribute order in the div. `video_attrs` d