in youtube-dl (older version, since this is youtube_dl not yt-dlp):\n\n```python\n    def _sort_formats(self, formats, field_preference=None):\n        if not formats:\n            return\n        if field_preference:\n            formats.sort(key=lambda f: tuple(\n                f.get(field) if f.get(field) is not None else -1\n                for field in field_preference))\n            return\n        for f in formats:\n            if f.get('preference') is None:\n                f['preference'] = ...\n```\n\nHmm, older youtube-dl:\n\n```python\n    def _sort_formats(self, formats, field_preference=None):\n        if not formats:\n            return\n        if field_preference:\n            def _format_key(f):\n                return tuple(f.get(field) if f.get(field) is not None else (-1, '') ...)\n```\n\nI really need to check. Let me include get_info('InfoExtractor._sort_formats').\n\nActually, you know what \u2014 there's a risk that real `_sort_formats` raises on formats missing keys (e.g., comparing None with int). In older youtube-dl:\n\n```python\n    def _sort_formats(self, formats, field_preference=None):\n        if not formats:\n            return\n        if field_preference:\n            def _format_key(f):\n                return tuple(\n                    f.get(field) if f.get(field) is not None else (-1, '')\n                    for field in field_preference)\n        else:\n            def _format_key(f):\n                return (\n                    f.get('preference') if f.get('preference') is not None else -1,\n                    f.get('width') if f.get('width') is not None else -1,\n                    f.get('height') if f.get('height') is not None else -1,\n                    f.get('tbr') if f.get('tbr') is not None else -1,\n                    f.get('vcodec'),\n                    f.get('acodec'),\n                    ...\n                )\n        formats.sort(key=_format_key)\n```\n\nComparing tuples with mixed types could raise 