econd \u2192 item WebPage \u2192 138 falsy; third \u2192 TVEpisode \u2192 line 139-140 \u2192 _json_ld returns None \u2192 info = {}. Covers everything in one test! And assert calls.json_ld_calls == [{'@type': 'TVEpisode', '@context': 'http://schema.org'}]. \n\nWait, but the item dict passed to _json_ld \u2014 the code does `item['@context'] = 'http://schema.org'` mutating the parsed dict, then calls `_json_ld(item, ...)`. So the recorded call arg should be the item dict with @context added. Since it's the same object mutated, my recorded reference will show @context. Good assertion.\n\nSo tests:\n\n1. `test_real_extract_full_pipeline` \u2014 main path, all main branches, thorough assertions.\n2. `test_real_extract_data_video_id_and_no_base` \u2014 line 60 or-fallback, line 104 falsy, line 118 or-[], line 135 json_ld falsy (no JSON-LD).\n3. `test_real_extract_non_breadcrumb_json_ld` \u2014 line 135 second operand falsy.\n4. `test_real_extract_search_json_ld_result` \u2014 line 131 falsy branch (skip fallback).\n5. `test_real_extract_breadcrumb_without_tvepisode_then_none` \u2014 lines 136-140 all branches including `or {}` on 140.\n\nAlso, should I cover `params['data-video-hmac']` KeyError? No \u2014 that's an error path, not needed for coverage.\n\nWhat about line 96 `video_data = ios_playlist['Playlist']['Video']` \u2014 covered in all tests.\n\nLine 145: `self._html_search_meta(['og:title', 'twitter:title'], webpage)` \u2014 real. If no meta tags, returns None. In tests with meta tags, returns the title. Fine.\n\nLine 149: `clean_html(get_element_by_class('episode-info__synopsis', webpage))` \u2014 real. With the div present, returns text. In test 2, maybe omit the synopsis div \u2192 returns None (clean_html(None) \u2192 None). Actually clean_html(None) returns None. That covers... well, line 149 executes either way. Fine.\n\nNow \u2014 one important detail: `_real_extract` is called directly. Normally you'd call `ie.extract(url)` which does `_match_id` etc. But `extract` does more (suitable check, report, etc.). Calling `_real_extract` directly is the standard approach for such unit tests. But wait \u2014 `_real_extract` calls `self._match_id(url)` and `self._download_webpage(url, video_id)` \u2014 all mocked/real fine.\n\nHmm, but `self._downloader` is None \u2014 do any called methods use `self._downloader`? `_download_webpage` (mocked) would. `_to_screen` etc. \u2014 not called in this path since downloads are mocked. `_search_regex` \u2014 uses `self._downloader` only for error reporting when fatal... If regex fails and default given, no error. OK.\n\n`_html_search_meta` \u2014 on failure (expected_type...), it calls `_html_search_regex` with fatal=False? Let me check: `_html_search_meta(name, html, display_name=None, fatal=False, **kwargs)` \u2014 default fatal=False. Returns None if not found. Fine.\n\n`_search_json_ld` \u2014 mocked. `_json_ld` \u2014 mocked. `_parse_json` \u2014 real, fine.\n\n`_sort_formats` \u2014 decide after get_info.\n\n`geo_verification_headers` \u2014 real, fine.\n\nNow, about imports: the test file needs `from youtube_dl.extractor.itv import ITVIE`. The code snippet given starts with imports `from youtube_dl.utils import clean_html, ...` \u2014 those are inside itv.py presumably. My test imports ITVIE from the extractor module.\n\nPotential issue: does `youtube_dl.extractor.itv` exist in the environment? Presumably yes since the code was \"extracted from youtube_dl/extractor/itv.py\". I'll import it. If ITVIE has `_VALID_URL`, great.\n\nLet me also double-check: `ITVIE` might have `_geo_bypass`... `geo_verification_headers` in newer youtube-dl:\n\n```python\n    def geo_verification_headers(self):\n        headers = {}\n        geo_proxy = self._get_geo_proxy()\n        if geo_proxy:\n            headers['X-Forwarded-For'] = geo_proxy\n        return headers\n```\n\n`_get_geo_proxy`:\n\n```python\n    def _get_geo_proxy(self):\n        if self._geo_proxy:\n            return self._geo_proxy\n        return None  # or reads config\n```\n\nHmm, older:\n\n```python\n    def _get_geo_proxy(self):\n        \"\"\"Return the location of a random proxy used by _download_webpage etc.\"\"\"\n        ...\n```\n\nMight read `self._downloader.params`... `self._downloader` is None! If `_get_geo_proxy` does `self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass_proxy')` \u2192 AttributeError on None. Hmm. Let me check `geo_verification_headers` and `_get_geo_proxy` via get_info. If risky, I can monkeypatch `geo_verification_headers` too... but that would skip line 62's call (still executes the line though). Or set `ie._downloader` to a fake with params dict. Or set `ie._x_forwarded_for_ip`/`_geo_proxy` attribute. Let me check the source first.\n\nActually, in youtube-dl (the original), `geo_verification_headers`:\n\n```python\n    def geo_verification_headers(self):\n        headers = {}\n        geo_proxy = self._get_geo_proxy()\n        if geo_proxy:\n            headers['X-Forwarded-For'] = geo_proxy\n        return headers\n```\n\nand\n\n```python\n    def _get_geo_proxy(self):\n        \"\"\"Return the location of a random proxy used by _download_webpage etc.\n        Returns None if there is no proxy.\"\"\"\n        if self._downloader:\n            return self._downloader.params.get('geo_bypass_proxy')\n        return None\n```\n\nHmm, not sure. Or maybe:\n\n```python\n    def _get_geo_proxy(self):\n        if self._geo_proxy:\n            return self._geo_proxy\n```\n\nwhere `self._geo_proxy` set in __init__:\n\n```python\n        self._geo_proxy = None\n        up = params.get('geo_bypass_proxy')\n        if up:\n            ...\n```\n\nWith downloader=None, params... `InfoExtractor.__init__(self, downloader=None)`: `self._downloader = downloader`. And does it read params? If downloader is None, `params = getattr(downloader, 'params', {})`? Hmm. Let me just check.\n\nOK, enough speculation \u2014 time to call get_info. Batch:\n\n1. get_info('ITVIE')\n2. get_info('InfoExtractor._match_id')\n3. get_info('InfoExtractor.geo_verification_headers')\n4. get_info('InfoExtractor._get_geo_proxy')\n5. get_info('InfoExtractor._sort_formats')\n6. get_info('InfoExtractor._search_json_ld')\n7. get_info('InfoExtractor._json_ld')\n8. get_info('InfoExtractor._download_json')\n9. get_info('InfoExtractor._extract_m3u8_formats')\n10. get_info('JSON_LD_RE')\n11. get_info('merge_dicts')\n12. get_info('parse_duration')\n13. get_info('InfoExtractor._html_search_meta')\n14. get_info('InfoExtractor._search_regex')\n15. get_info('InfoExtractor._parse_json')\n16. get_info('InfoExtractor._download_webpage')\n\nThat's 16 calls. Maybe trim to the essential ones to keep it manageable: ITVIE, _match_id, geo_verification_headers, _get_geo_proxy, _sort_formats, _search_json_ld, _json_ld, JSON_LD_RE, merge_dicts, parse_duration, _html_search_meta, _download_json. That's 12. I'll include _extract_m3u8_formats too to know its signature for the mock. And _search_regex to confirm default/group behavior. OK let me do ~14 calls in one block.\n\nAfter that, write the final test.\n\nLet me pre-draft the test file now, and adjust after the tool results.\n\n```python\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"Coverage tests for youtube_dl.extractor.itv.ITVIE._real_extract.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom youtube_dl.extractor.itv import ITVIE\n\n\nHUB_URL = 'https://www.itv.com/hub/a-test-show/2a1234a'\n\nMETA_AND_SYNOPSIS = u'''\n<head><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Test Episode Title\"></head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"video\" data-video-playlist=\"https://m.itv.com/playlist/2a1234a\" data-video-hmac=\"aabbccdd\"></div>\n<div class=\"episode-info__synopsis\">A test synopsis</div>\n</body>\n'''\n\ndef _webpage(video_tag_attrs, json_ld=None, title='Test Episode Title', synopsis='A test synopsis'):\n    ...\n```\n\nHmm, building webpages via string templates. Let me define a few module-level constants instead \u2014 simpler and clearer.\n\nLet me write it:\n\n```python\nimport json\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom youtube_dl.extractor.itv import ITVIE\n\n\ndef _make_webpage(video_attrs, json_ld_scripts=(), title='Test Episode Title',\n                  synopsis='A test synopsis'):\n    attrs = ' '.join('%s=\"%s\"' % (k, v) for k, v in video_attrs.items())\n    parts = [\n        u'<!DOCTYPE html><html><head>',\n        u'<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"%s\">' % title,\n        u'</head><body>',\n        u'<div id=\"video\" %s></div>' % attrs,\n    ]\n    if synopsis is not None:\n        parts.append(u'<div class=\"episode-info__synopsis\">%s</div>' % synopsis)\n    for script in json_ld_scripts:\n        parts.append(\n            u'<script type=\"application/ld+json\">%s</script>' % script)\n    parts.append(u'</body></html>')\n    return u'\\n'.join(parts)\n```\n\nAnd a playlist builder:\n\n```python\ndef _make_playlist(video=None):\n    return {'Playlist': {'Video': video if video is not None else {}}}\n```\n\nAnd the fakes installer:\n\n```python\nclass _Record(object):\n    pass\n\n\ndef _patch_ie(monkeypatch, webpage, playlist, search_json_ld=None,\n              json_ld_result=None, m3u8_formats=None):\n    rec = _Record()\n    rec.webpage_urls = []\n    rec.playlist_requests = []\n    rec.m3u8_calls = []\n    rec.json_ld_calls = []\n    rec.sort_calls = []\n\n    def fake_download_webpage(url, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        rec.webpage_urls.append(url)\n        return webpage\n\n    def fake_download_json(url, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        rec.playlist_requests.append({\n            'url': url,\n            'video_id': video_id,\n            'data': kwargs.get('data'),\n            'headers': kwargs.get('headers'),\n        })\n        return playlist\n\n    def fake_extract_m3u8(url, video_id, ext=None, *args, **kwargs):\n        rec.m3u8_calls.append({'url': url, 'video_id': video_id, 'ext': ext,\n                               'kwargs': kwargs})\n        if m3u8_formats is not None:\n            return list(m3u8_