s(html_element)`:\n\n```python\ndef extract_attributes(html_element):\n    \"\"\"Return a dict of attributes of a HTML element.\"\"\"\n    return {k: v for k, v in re.findall(r'([a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+)\\s*=\\s*([\"\\'])(.*?)\\2', html_element)}\n```\n\nHmm, roughly. Actually:\n\n```python\ndef extract_attributes(html_element):\n    \"\"\"Return a dict of attributes of a HTML element.\n    ...\n    \"\"\"\n    return dict(re.findall(r'''(?xs)\n        \\s([a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+)\\s*=\\s*\n        (?:\n            (?P<q>[\"'])(?P<v1>.*?)(?P=q)|\n            (?P<v2>[^\\s\"'>]+)\n        )''', html_element))\n```\n\nSomething like that. Works on the tag string. Good.\n\nNote: the regex `<[^>]+id=\"video\"[^>]*>` \u2014 `[^>]+` before `id=\"video\"` \u2014 so `<div ` then `id=\"video\"` \u2014 the `[^>]+` matches `div `. Good. But careful: attribute order \u2014 `id` must appear; my div has id first. Good.\n\nNow, JSON-LD scripts in the webpage \u2014 careful that the JSON-LD script content doesn't contain `</script>` prematurely. Fine.\n\nAlso careful: the `_search_regex(r'(?s)(<[^>]+id=\"video\"[^>]*>)', ...)` \u2014 with `(?s)`, `[^>]` still excludes '>'. Fine.\n\nOne more: in test 4, `_search_json_ld` returns non-empty \u2192 fallback skipped. But the webpage for test 4 \u2014 I'll include a BreadcrumbList JSON-LD script to prove it's NOT consumed (rec.json_ld_calls == []). \n\nNow let me also think: do I need `pytest` import at all if I only use monkeypatch fixture? I don't need `import pytest` unless I use pytest.mark or raises. I'll keep it minimal \u2014 maybe no pytest import needed. Actually, no top-level code beyond imports/constants/functions. Fine.\n\nWait, the instructions: \"Write as little top-level code as possible\" \u2014 module-level constants and helper functions are fine; just no pytest.main calls.\n\nLet me also consider: should tests be in a class? Plain functions are fine.\n\nNow let me also double check `_match_id` behavior with my URL. If `_VALID_URL = r'htt